  "notes": "The National Heritage Board documents a two-floor tropical villa with an open, curved porte-cochère and upper sitting room, Corinthian columns, cast iron railings, ornate arched openings, storey cornices, louvre shutters and filigree eaves. Its historical account identifies the later rear extension. Official trail text identifies overlapping orange-brown roof tiles."
